WEBVTT

00:00:04.349 --> 00:00:10.650
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Wednesday the sixteenth. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the silent-film thing again?</v>

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:20.870
<v Aisha Begum>You're on. I was just saying, weekend plans are looking a bit soggy. Supposed to be walking, but have you seen the weather?</v>

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:28.539
<v Grace Liu>It's Wednesday. Plenty of time for the forecast to be wrong in three different ways.</v>

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:36.359
<v Hannah Price>While we're on important matters, whose new car is that in the car park? Very brave, parking something that shiny here.</v>

00:00:38.679 --> 00:00:42.880
<v Callum Reid>Not mine. Mine's the one with the protective coating of factory dust.</v>

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.049
<v Marcus Hale>Anyone see the football last night? Honestly, ninety minutes I'm never getting back.</v>

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:53.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we lose another ninety. Where are we with yesterday's bits?</v>

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.899
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, tested the BFP yesterday and it's all fine now. That testing's done.</v>

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:05.120
<v Aisha Begum>That's yesterday's test you're closing out, yeah? Not another test on today's list?</v>

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.120
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Exactly. Completed work, not a fresh job.</v>

00:01:09.329 --> 00:01:15.280
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And I already swapped the filter on the PRV on the boiler yesterday. That's finished as well.</v>

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:20.340
<v Grace Liu>Right, so that filter change isn't still hanging over us?</v>

00:01:22.079 --> 00:01:25.930
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, all done. Just making sure it doesn't get counted twice.</v>

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:32.780
<v Hannah Price>One observation from nights: noticed the Water Booster Pump was running a bit warm, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:34.709 --> 00:01:39.959
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, the settled-down bit's worth saying. Otherwise that sounds rather more exciting than it was.</v>

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.950
<v Hannah Price>Exactly. Just an observation, not raising another job off it.</v>

00:01:46.379 --> 00:01:53.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Pricey, can you check the guarding on the stacker by 11am? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:59.239
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll check the guarding on the stacker. I've got that.</v>

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.739
<v Grace Liu>And that's the production hold we're talking about, rather than a routine look round?</v>

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:09.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes. It's holding production up, so that check is right at the front.</v>

00:02:11.659 --> 00:02:14.110
<v Hannah Price>Understood. By 11am, not sometime before lunch.</v>

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:24.460
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah, can you also investigate the pressure drop on the boiler feed pump, today at 2pm? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:32.389
<v Hannah Price>Right, um, both production blockers with me, then? Just making sure I haven't heard two different versions of first.</v>

00:02:33.259 --> 00:02:40.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Both are ahead of routine work. The guarding has the earlier deadline, by 11am; the pressure-drop investigation is today at 2pm.</v>

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:47.860
<v Hannah Price>Okay, I'll investigate the pressure drop on the boiler feed pump, today at 2pm. Those two take priority.</v>

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:57.449
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Just to separate that from what I said earlier—yesterday's BFP test was fine. I'm not saying that explains away this pressure drop.</v>

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:04.009
<v Hannah Price>Yep, understood. The investigation's still needed; I'm not assuming a cause from yesterday's result.</v>

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:11.590
<v Sarah Okafor>Haley, can you send the shift handover report round today at 2pm? Normal priority on that.</v>

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:18.469
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round today at 2pm. Fine by me.</v>

00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:23.969
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, you clipped a bit there. Two, was it?</v>

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:29.789
<v Sarah Okafor>Two, yes, today at 2pm. Normal priority, not an emergency shout.</v>

00:03:30.389 --> 00:03:34.590
<v Marcus Hale>Got it. Teams picked a good moment to eat half a sentence.</v>

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:42.909
<v Callum Reid>On the blocked stuff, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the spinner. Nothing's changed there.</v>

00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:49.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, still blocked. We're not adding a new chasing job in this meeting.</v>

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:59.729
<v Callum Reid>And we were going to replace the belt on the newer turbine, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it.</v>

00:04:00.219 --> 00:04:03.370
<v Aisha Begum>So definitely not part of today's work, that belt?</v>

00:04:04.409 --> 00:04:08.610
<v Callum Reid>Definitely not. Off today's list, not something we're trying to squeeze in.</v>

00:04:10.949 --> 00:04:17.949
<v Callum Reid>The live one for me—I'll take vibration readings on the turbine one compressor by Thursday. Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:04:19.269 --> 00:04:23.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, Reidy. The turbine one compressor readings are your drop-everything job.</v>

00:04:24.279 --> 00:04:27.779
<v Callum Reid>Yep. By Thursday, and ahead of my less urgent stuff.</v>

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:34.569
<v Grace Liu>Right. Different from the belt that's been pushed out. Easy to mash those together when everyone's talking.</v>

00:04:36.529 --> 00:04:42.829
<v Callum Reid>Yeah. And I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team for Monday. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:45.089 --> 00:04:49.290
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Reidy. Toolbox talk for Monday agreed, without bumping the vibration readings.</v>

00:04:51.389 --> 00:04:54.189
<v Callum Reid>That's it. Important, but not a drop-everything one.</v>

00:04:56.180 --> 00:05:02.480
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah, can you recalibrate the sensors on the relief valve tomorrow morning? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:11.420
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, no, I can't take that as well. With the guarding and pressure-drop investigation already with me, I haven't got room for it.</v>

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:20.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Reidy, can you take that instead—recalibrate the sensors on the relief valve tomorrow morning? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:20.629 --> 00:05:25.879
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll take that instead. I'll recalibrate the sensors on the relief valve tomorrow morning.</v>

00:05:27.209 --> 00:05:35.610
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And just so nobody hears 'valve' and crosses off the wrong thing, my completed bit was the filter on the PRV on the boiler.</v>

00:05:37.939 --> 00:05:43.540
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, separate things. That filter swap is finished; this sensor recalibration has just gone to Reidy.</v>

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:51.519
<v Callum Reid>Got it. Tomorrow morning for the relief valve sensors. Matters, but it's not urgent; the vibration readings keep the drop-everything priority.</v>

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:57.100
<v Grace Liu>And the toolbox talk is Monday, not something you're trying to fit in this morning?</v>

00:05:57.699 --> 00:06:00.149
<v Callum Reid>Monday, yes. I'll organise it for then.</v>

00:06:00.899 --> 00:06:04.399
<v Marcus Hale>Mine's straightforward: handover report round today at 2pm, normal priority.</v>

00:06:05.269 --> 00:06:14.720
<v Hannah Price>And I've got the guarding on the stacker by 11am, then the pressure drop on the boiler feed pump, today at 2pm. Not the relief valve calibration.</v>

00:06:16.879 --> 00:06:20.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Both your production-blocking jobs stay ahead of routine work.</v>

00:06:22.589 --> 00:06:25.389
<v Aisha Begum>Lovely. That's clearer than my weekend forecast, anyway.</v>

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:29.470
<v Grace Liu>Your weekend forecast is waterproof trousers and disappointment.</v>

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, any confusion left before we finish?</v>

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:40.100
<v Olumide Adeyemi>None here. Mine were completed updates only, nothing new for today.</v>

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:47.060
<v Callum Reid>All clear. The spinner delivery's still blocked, and the newer turbine belt isn't back on today's list.</v>

00:06:48.649 --> 00:06:50.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. That's us, then. Thanks, everyone.</v>
